From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 10:40:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 11/22] fix(kernel): avoid undersized TLSF free blocks

A split block must have enough payload for the two pointers in free_node_t.
Checking only for room beyond hdr_t can leave a four-byte payload on 32-bit
targets. INSERT_FREE_BLOCK then writes its eight-byte free-list node across
the following physical block header.

Require both the block header and a complete free-list node before splitting.
---
 rom/kernel/tlsf.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/rom/kernel/tlsf.c b/rom/kernel/tlsf.c
--- a/rom/kernel/tlsf.c
+++ b/rom/kernel/tlsf.c
@@ -704,7 +704,8 @@ void * tlsf_malloc(struct MemHeaderExt *mhe, IPTR size, ULONG *flags)
     REMOVE_HEADER(mhe, tlsf, b, fl, sl);
 
     /* Is this block larger then requested? Try to split it then */
-    if (likely(GET_SIZE(b) > (size + ROUNDUP(sizeof(hdr_t)))))
+    if (likely(GET_SIZE(b) >= (size + ROUNDUP(sizeof(hdr_t)) +
+                               ROUNDUP(sizeof(free_node_t)))))
     {
         /* New split block */
         bhdr_t *sb = GET_NEXT_BHDR(b, size);
